// Source: Source: Fuenfzig Kinderlieder (1843), No.43 Biene, upper vocal staff. https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Summ_summ_summ.jpg
// Expanded instrumental arrangement. The established melody keeps all pitches, onsets, written durations, rests, tempo and meter. Original plucked/keyboard accompaniment remains; independent low strings sustain its bass line and violin/viola voice its explicitly simultaneous harmonies. Common chord tones are tied, not reattacked. Characteristic triangle percussion marks phrase/rhythmic structure. No choir is used. Standard GM/CC7=100; lead and accompaniment velocities balanced for the larger ensemble.
// Musicbox title: Summ%2C%20summ%2C%20summ
